From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:58:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] arm64: dts: apple: t7001-air2: Give each light sensor its
 position

The iPad Air 2 has both of the CT819s its device tree lists, and its
LSCI calibration holds one record per sensor. iOS gives each sensor the
record of its placement and orientation, the IOHIDPlacementType and
IOHIDOrientationType of its ADT node: 1 and 6 for als1 at 0x49, 1 and 5
for als2 at 0x29 (J81 and J82, iPadOS 15.8.8). Describe them, so that
tsl2583 picks the same record.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi | 18 ++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
index a1f97b4..725e466 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
@@ -267,12 +267,14 @@
 };
 
 /*
- * The ambient light sensor: a CT819 on i2c2. The device trees of the J81
- * and J82 list it twice, as i2c2/als1 at 0x49 (interrupt GPIO 103) and
- * i2c2/als2 at 0x29 (interrupt GPIO 110), both "probe-for-hardware": iOS
- * uses the one that answers. Both are described; the absent one fails its
- * chip ID read. Both name the unit's SysCfg LSCI record as alsCalibration,
- * which the loader copies into each through the als0 and als1 aliases.
+ * The ambient light sensors: two CT819s on i2c2. The device trees of the
+ * J81 and J82 list i2c2/als1 at 0x49 (interrupt GPIO 103, orientation 6)
+ * and i2c2/als2 at 0x29 (interrupt GPIO 110, orientation 5), both
+ * "probe-for-hardware"; a J81 has both. Both name the unit's SysCfg LSCI
+ * record set as alsCalibration, which the loader copies into each through
+ * the als0 and als1 aliases. It holds one record per sensor, and each
+ * sensor takes the one of its placement and orientation (the ADT's
+ * IOHIDPlacementType and IOHIDOrientationType), as iOS does.
  * i2c2 has nothing else on it.
  */
 &i2c2 {
@@ -283,6 +285,8 @@
 		compatible = "apple,ct819", "amstaos,tsl2581";
 		reg = <0x29>;
 		interrupts-extended = <&pinctrl 110 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+		apple,als-placement = <1>;
+		apple,als-orientation = <5>;
 	};
 
 	/* m1n1 adds apple,als-calibration from the ADT */
@@ -290,6 +294,8 @@
 		compatible = "apple,ct819", "amstaos,tsl2581";
 		reg = <0x49>;
 		interrupts-extended = <&pinctrl 103 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+		apple,als-placement = <1>;
+		apple,als-orientation = <6>;
 	};
 };
 
